{"type":"text","timestamp":1794561651502,"sessionID":"ses_e2bccad09ffe2W451DarRh6OXK","part":{"id":"prt_1d4359edd001CyZ9zM8MQo0tZv","sessionID":"ses_e2bccad09ffe2W451DarRh6OXK","messageID":"msg_1d435829e001ytMcUTwfP6sQwm","type":"text","text":"**T062 complete.**\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` only (untracked before and after, verified with read-only `git status --short`). The `lib/subprocess.ts` modification visible in status predates this task and was not touched.\n\n**Change**\n- Replaced `bounds stderr from a child that floods it and exits non-zero` with `stops reading stderr at the cap, so a busy marker past it is not seen`.\n- Its script waits for stdin end, writes 1 MiB of `e`, then `\\ndatabase is locked\\n`, and exits 1.\n- Asserts `ok === false`, `errorCode === 'NON_ZERO_EXIT'`, `retriesAttempted === 0`.\n- Added the comment above the case: the returned stderr is cut short whatever the cap, so the retry decision is the one reading that shows where collection stopped.\n- Removed the local `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS` because no remaining case reads it.\n- Kept the stdout case. No change to `SUB`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n   Start at  10:20:16\n   Duration  400ms (transform 114ms, setup 31ms, import 120ms, tests 98ms, environment 0ms)\n```\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"database is locked\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts\n1\n\n$ rg -c \"toBeLessThanOrEqual\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts\n(no output, exit 1)\n```\n\n**Why the case fails without the cap:** without `capOutput` on stderr, the full stream is collected, `SQLITE_BUSY_PATTERN` matches the `database is locked` marker that lands after the first MiB, and the call retries once and returns `SQLITE_BUSY_EXHAUSTED` with `retriesAttempted: 1`. With the cap, collection stops at 1 MiB before that marker, so the marker is never seen and the result is the script's own `NON_ZERO_EXIT` with no retry. The old stderr case could not show this because `sanitizeStderr` truncates the returned value to 240 characters either way, so its length assertion passed with or without the cap. The cap was already present, and I did not remove it or touch git state.\n\nCheckbox left unticked as instructed. Nothing was blocked.","time":{"start":1794561646301,"end":1794561651502}}}
